eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-12 : List Word
eye-contact-co-processing-at-the-speed-of-light-12 = unlines (cons "In “Eye Contact: Co-Processing at the Speed of Light” (Part 7 of the Information Dynamic series), on eye contact, the coupling through light of two people's nervous systems, as mutual influence:" (cons "Co-Processors: Mutual Influence" (cons "The coupling isn't one-way observation. It's bidirectional simultaneous co-processing:" (cons "Each person's nervous system:" (cons "Observes other's state (via photon flux from their body)" (cons "Forms quotient (compressed model of their internal state)" (cons "Updates own state based on model (emotional contagion, social influence, coordination)" (cons "Modulates behavior (conscious and unconscious responses)" (cons "Becomes observable to other (who updates their model)" (cons "The feedback creates emergent dynamics:" (cons "Two people making eye contact aren't just two separate observers. They're coupled system—each nervous system is input to the other's processing, creating feedback loop that shapes both." (cons "Examples:" (cons "Emotional contagion: Seeing someone smile activates mirror neurons, induces similar state" (cons "Coordination: Observing their gaze direction orients your attention (joint attention)" (cons "Dominance/submission: Extended mutual gaze creates tension resolved by one looking away" (cons "Attraction: Pupil dilation in one person triggers dilation in other (positive feedback)" (cons "The co-processing can produce states neither person would reach independently. The coupling creates temporary unified system (while maintaining distinct boundaries) that processes information jointly." nil)))))))))))))))))
